Reset the payload cursor when reusing an accumulator for the next capsule.
Without this, a shorter second capsule underflows the memcpy length and a
longer one retains bytes from the preceding payload.

Applies to picoquic 55b473e207e436d06ea9a2895cc1fc555d42c81c.
Regression: adapters/pico_wt/tests/test_pico_wt_capsule_sequence.c.

diff --git a/picohttp/h3zero_common.c b/picohttp/h3zero_common.c
--- a/picohttp/h3zero_common.c
+++ b/picohttp/h3zero_common.c
@@ -2115,6 +2115,7 @@ const uint8_t* h3zero_accumulate_capsule(const uint8_t* bytes, const uint8_t* bytes_max, h3zero_capsule_t* capsule)
 		/* reset the fields to expected value */
 		capsule->header_length = 0;
 		capsule->header_read = 0;
+		capsule->value_read = 0;
 		capsule->capsule_type = 0;
 		capsule->capsule_length = 0;
 		capsule->is_stored = 0;
